extraction_notes: "PLAYABILITY: the heading on printed 181 reads An Optional Player Character R.C.C., and the entry says the unprincipled, anarchist and aberrant vampires are the types most likely to be player characters; survey D3 lists it among the entries tagged optional. SOURCE: the entry''s own stats run printed 181-182; the shared powers it cites (See Vampire Powers Section) are printed 183-187, and the Master Vampire it is measured against is printed 179-180 (excluded by D3). EXPERIENCE: the ladder is ''Nightprince & Vampire'' on printed 233, read off a render: 0, 5,001, 10,001, 20,001, 40,001, 80,001, 120,001, 160,001, 200,001, 250,001, 300,001, 400,000 (sic, not 400,001), 500,001, 600,001, 1,000,000 (printed ''1 Million''), top of level 15 at 2 Million; level 1 prints its upper bound as 5000 without a comma. NOT stored in xp_table, per the class-import rule that no R.C.C. carries one; recorded here for the lead. The entry''s Experience Level line (2nd to 7th, 1D6+1) is an NPC level; player characters start at first level. HIT POINTS AND S.D.C.: printed 181 gives the equivalent of 3D4x10 hit points and no S.D.C.; the Master Vampire''s entry (printed 180) explains vampires are nearly impervious to all weapons. Stored as hit_points_base 3d4x10 with no per-level gain (none is printed) and sdc_base 0, stated so the character gets no S.D.C. rather than the printed 36 default. I.S.P.: NOT PRINTED. The entry calls the secondary vampire a major psionic and grants the vampire powers, but prints no I.S.P. line, unlike the Master (3D6x10, printed 180) and the Wild Vampire (1D6x10, printed 183); confirmed on a render of printed 182. isp_base is absent rather than borrowed from the Master. PSIONICS: the ten powers of printed 185 are granted by name, all equal to a fourth level psionic (prose); Alter Aura (Self) is the catalog''s Alter Aura. Super-Hypnotic Suggestion (20 I.S.P., printed 185, exclusive to vampires) is named as its own row; its stat block is also carried in natural_abilities. MIND CONTROL OVER VAMPIRES and the TELEPATHIC LINK (printed 184-185) are automatic and cost no I.S.P., so they are abilities, not powers. The link is worded for a master vampire and its creations; it is kept here because printed 181 gives the secondary vampire all the supernatural powers of the master, and a secondary vampire has creations of its own. COMBAT: five attacks stored as attacks_base; the two-psionic-plus-one alternative is prose. BONUSES: +3 save vs magic or psionic mind control is stored as saves.mind_control. SKILLS: printed 182 says the average secondary vampire retains ten skills and gains two more at levels 3, 6, 9, 11 and 13, all at first level proficiency and never increasing, from Communication, Domestic, Piloting, Technical, Rogue, Wilderness and Weapon Proficiencies. The ten are a choice group with per_level 0 and no bonus. The later picks are stored as a related-skill schedule with a count of 0 and the same categories; the book''s ''do not increase'' is NOT stored for them, only noted - a related pick advances at the catalog rate. Horsemanship is a Pilot skill in this book and its own catalog category, so Horsemanship: General is offered by name (the Ashmedai precedent); Pilot Related is a separate category in this book and is not offered. No related or secondary skill list beyond this is printed. SLOW KILL: printed 181 says 58% of a secondary vampire''s slow kill victims become wild vampires; the table on printed 184 gives 45-00, which is 56%. The table is stored. The human-slave limit (one for a secondary vampire) is printed 184. NIGHTVISION: named in the Master''s Natural Abilities line on printed 180, with no range anywhere in the vampire section. MAGIC: prints no P.P.E. growth; retained spells from a former life are prose. EQUIPMENT AND MONEY: none printed; the entry says secondary vampires rely on natural powers, at most driving a car or rarely using a gun. No Talents and no Horror Factor bonus beyond the printed 12."
